Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow boards to disable firmware MLO

CS-06 dumps show a NULL peer dereference in the WLAN.WBE.1.6 partner
UMAC migration path. Provide a board opt-out as a compatibility workaround;
it does not repair the closed firmware's NULL-peer handling.

Keep the WSI group intact for fixed-memory ownership and coordinated
recovery. Honor qcom,ath12k-disable-mlo on any member before selecting
single-chip or multi-chip MLO, including on recovery. The existing MAC
allocator then registers one wiphy per radio.

Advertise an explicit disabled MLO capability to firmware. Return no
partner links when MLO is disabled so the ready and teardown paths do not
send MLO commands just because the WSI group still contains two devices.
Boards without the opt-out retain their existing MLO capability selection.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1124,6 +1124,9 @@
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&ag->mutex);
 
+	if (!ag->mlo_capable)
+		return 0;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ag->num_devices; i++) {
 		partner_ab = ag->ab[i];
 
@@ -2318,6 +2321,21 @@
 
 	lockdep_assert_held(&ag->mutex);
 
+	/* Retain WSI grouping for shared memory and reset coordination, while
+	 * allowing boards with incompatible partner firmware to use separate
+	 * non-MLO wiphys. Recheck the policy on every firmware start.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < ag->num_devices; i++) {
+		ab = ag->ab[i];
+		if (ab && of_property_read_bool(ab->dev->of_node,
+					     "qcom,ath12k-disable-mlo")) {
+			ag->mlo_capable = false;
+			ath12k_info(ab, "WSI group %d: MLO disabled by board policy\n",
+				    ag->id);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (ag->num_devices == 1) {
 		ab = ag->ab[0];
 		/* QCN9274 firmware uses firmware IE for MLO advertisement */
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2225,8 +2225,11 @@
 	int i, j, ret;
 
 	if (!ag->mlo_capable) {
+		/* An absent optional TLV does not explicitly disable firmware MLO. */
+		req->mlo_capable_valid = 1;
+		req->mlo_capable = 0;
 		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_QMI,
-			   "MLO is disabled hence skip QMI MLO cap");
+			   "MLO disabled, advertise QMI capability 0\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
 
